      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The pueblo consists of three villages—Rebahene, Ranchitos, and Chicale—forming its core community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://santaana-nsn.gov/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A historic north‑south trade route along the Rio Grande skirted Santa Ana, keeping it one of the state’s least visited pueblos.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://santaana-nsn.gov/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The cacique, a priest‑like leader, ensures order, authorizes communal rituals, and appoints key officials.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
